  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14226474/assets/93489f5dd12c8dbbde799b4047965a89e4204f151c0b4dfc36286392775a05e2.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{3}{4},$ calculate the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above.",
  "worked_solution": "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{3}{4},$ where $\\theta =m∠C.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ adjacent to $∠C.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to find the length of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{AB}{AC} \\\\ \\frac{3}{4} & =\\frac{AB}{8} \\\\ AB & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot 8 \\\\ AB & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot AB \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
